      <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.3;">Sustainable Clothing Manufacturers — Beyond the Marketing</h1>
      
      <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; max-width: 800px;">Most clothing labeled "sustainable" in 2026 has no verifiable proof. Here's how to find manufacturers whose claims hold up to scrutiny.</p>
      
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 800px;">The fashion industry spent an estimated $750 billion on sustainability marketing in 2025. Less than 25% of brands making environmental claims could provide third-party verification when challenged. The gap between marketing and reality has become so significant that regulators worldwide are cracking down. The EU Green Claims Directive, FTC Green Guides update in 2024, and UK CMA greenwashing actions signal the end of unchecked sustainability claims.</p>
      
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 800px;">"Sustainable" in marketing terms means whatever a brand wants it to mean. In regulatory terms, it requires specific certifications, traceability, and third-party verification. This guide separates marketing from reality. Brands need to know the difference — buyers pay the price when greenwashing claims collapse under scrutiny.</p>
      
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 800px;">We cover the verifiable pillars of sustainable manufacturing, the 2025-2026 regulatory wave reshaping the industry, how certifications actually work, manufacturers with publicly verifiable credentials, and a verification protocol buyers can use to test any claim. The cost of greenwashing is paid by future buyers — not the brands selling it today.</p>
      
      <a href="#verified-manufacturers" style="display: inline-block; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; background: #e00; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500;">Skip to Verified Manufacturers</a>
    </div>
  </section>

